# REMUS-100 ArduSub defaults (Phase C-fallback, 2026-08-08).
#
# Provenance: NOT the DAVE BlueROV2 config (vehicle_twins/auv_vulnerable_bluerov2's
# defaults come from ~/auv_ws/src/dave/models/dave_robot_models/config/bluerov2/
# ardusub.parm), which the project's own plan explicitly flags as loaded with
# BlueROV2-hardware-specific junk (camera mount, joystick buttons, that
# specific unit's compass/accelerometer calibration offsets, a rangefinder
# REMUS's model doesn't have) that would misrepresent a REMUS-100 twin if
# carried over unedited. Every line below is either (a) kept because it's
# load-bearing for THIS vehicle's own SDF/EKF setup, confirmed by reading
# this project's own attacks/acoustic_spoof.py and the SERVO_FUNCTION <->
# model.sdf channel wiring directly, or (b) an ArduSub firmware default
# (from ardupilot/Tools/autotest/default_params/sub.parm) reasonable to
# inherit as a starting point. Dropped entirely, not carried over: BTN*
# (joystick button mapping -- REMUS isn't joystick-driven), COMPASS_OFS*/
# INS_ACC*OFFS/INS_ACC*SCAL (that specific BlueROV2 unit's sensor
# calibration bias), MNT_* (camera gimbal -- no camera mount on this
# model), RNGFND1_* (rangefinder -- no such sensor on this model; leaving
# it enabled with no backing sensor risks a bogus EKF/failsafe reading),
# SERVO8_* (camera tilt output -- no 8th channel on this model),
# BARO_EXT_BUS (physical I2C wiring, meaningless in SITL).

# Thruster output mapping: motor1..motor6 -> SERVO1..SERVO6, matching
# model.sdf's ArduPilotPlugin <control channel="0..5"> -> thruster1_joint.."
# .."thruster6_joint wiring exactly (same channel order BlueROV2 uses,
# confirmed directly against both SDFs).
SERVO1_FUNCTION 33
SERVO2_FUNCTION 34
SERVO3_FUNCTION 35
SERVO4_FUNCTION 36
SERVO5_FUNCTION 37
SERVO6_FUNCTION 38

BATT_MONITOR     4
FS_OPTIONS       0

# Use EK3 (ArduSub's modern default estimator).
EK2_ENABLE 0
EK3_ENABLE 1
AHRS_EKF_TYPE 3

# Underwater position source: REMUS-100, like BlueROV2, gets no GPS (RF
# doesn't penetrate water) -- its horizontal position comes from an
# acoustic positioning system (USBL/LBL/DVL), modeled here the same way
# this project already models it for BlueROV2: fed to ArduPilot as
# VISION_POSITION_ESTIMATE by attacks/acoustic_spoof.py (which now derives
# its Gazebo odometry topic from constants.MODEL_NAME instead of a
# hardcoded "bluerov2", so it works unmodified for this vehicle too).
# GPS_TYPE/SIM_GPS_* kept enabled for parity with BlueROV2's own baseline
# (harmless if EK3 doesn't end up using GPS as a source).
GPS_TYPE 1
SIM_GPS_DISABLE 0
SIM_GPS_LOCK 1
VISO_TYPE 1
EK3_SRC1_POSXY 6
EK3_SRC1_VELXY 6
EK3_SRC1_POSZ 1
EK3_SRC1_VELZ 6
EK3_SRC1_YAW 6
COMPASS_USE 0
COMPASS_USE2 0
COMPASS_USE3 0
SIM_BARO_RND 0.01

# Depth-hold (ALT_HOLD) position-controller gains: inherited starting
# point from the DAVE BlueROV2 config (ardupilot's own generic sub.parm
# uses renamed equivalents in a newer parameter tree not present in this
# project's built SITL binary -- confirmed these DAVE-style names are the
# ones this binary actually accepts, since they're what the already-
# working BlueROV2 twin uses). NOT re-tuned for REMUS-100's different
# mass/thrust ratio -- live-verify ALT_HOLD behavior before trusting depth
# control precision; retune here if it proves unstable.
PSC_ACCZ_P   2
PSC_ACCZ_I   4
PSC_ACCZ_FF  0.75
PSC_VELZ_P   8
PSC_POSZ_P   3
PSC_POSXY_P 2.5
PSC_VELXY_D 0.8
PSC_VELXY_I 0.5
PSC_VELXY_P 5.0
